@page "/privacy"

@* English-only for now, like the About page. *@

<PageTitle>Privacy Policy - Randomize</PageTitle>

<h2 class="page-title">Privacy</h2>

<div class="about-layout legal">

    <section class="about-card">
        <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: June 2026</p>
        <p>Randomize (userandomize.net) is a small hobby project. It has no accounts, no ads, and no tracking. This page explains the little data that's actually involved.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-card">
        <h3>Stored in your browser</h3>
        <p>Your preferences live in your browser's local storage and never leave your device: the theme and language you pick, motion and visual toggles, whether you've seen the welcome message, and any custom Rock-Paper-Scissors skins you upload. Uploaded skin images are kept only in your browser - they're never sent to a server. Clearing your site data removes all of it.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-card">
        <h3>No analytics or tracking</h3>
        <p>There are no analytics scripts, advertising networks, tracking pixels, or fingerprinting. Nothing here builds a profile of you.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-card">
        <h3>The contact form</h3>
        <p>If you send a message through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>, your message and the email address you provide are emailed to me so I can reply. They aren't shared, sold, or stored anywhere else. A Cloudflare Turnstile check guards the form against spam.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-card">
        <h3>Anonymous counts</h3>
        <p>The site keeps simple running totals - for example how many songs, movies, or games have been rolled overall. These are just numbers and contain no personal information.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-card">
        <h3>Hosting and third parties</h3>
        <p>The site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. As with any website, Cloudflare processes the requests needed to deliver pages and to rate-limit abuse, which can include your IP address, under Cloudflare's own terms.</p>
        <p>The randomizers fetch data and images from third-party services: Spotify (music and the embedded player), TMDB (films and TV), IGDB (games), and Riot Games' Data Dragon and Legends of Runeterra artwork (the League of Legends tools). The Spotify player is an embedded iframe that may set its own cookies and is governed by <a href="https://www.spotify.com/legal/privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Spotify's privacy policy</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-card">
        <h3>Children</h3>
        <p>Randomize isn't directed at children and doesn't knowingly collect information from them.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-card">
        <h3>Changes</h3>
        <p>This policy may change as the site evolves; the date above will be updated when it does. Questions? Reach me through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.</p>
        <p class="legal-nav"><a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> · <a href="/about">About</a></p>
    </section>

</div>
